# Security Rules

Clerk authenticates identity.
Application authorization determines capability.
Supabase RLS protects database rows.

Never trust client-provided user IDs, roles, plans, entitlements, ownership, prices, seller IDs or transaction totals.
Every protected API handler must authenticate and authorize independently.
Provider credentials remain server-side.
Webhook endpoints must verify signatures/secrets.
